---
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
---

<ProductLayout 
  title="AstroSurvey Q1" 
  tagline="Advanced Geospatial Mapping for Precision Analysis"
  productName="AstroSurvey Q1 Geospatial Mapping Drone"
  productPdf="AstroSurvey Q1 Geospatial Mapping Drone.docx"
  description="The AstroSurvey Q1 Geospatial Mapping Drone is engineered for high-precision aerial surveying and mapping applications. Integrating multispectral imaging, LiDAR technology, and precision positioning systems, the AstroSurvey Q1 delivers centimeter-level accuracy for detailed terrain analysis, volumetric calculations, and environmental monitoring. Designed for surveying professionals, urban planners, agricultural specialists, and environmental researchers, it combines long flight duration with sophisticated data processing to transform complex geospatial data into actionable insights."
>
  <div class="key-features">
    <h2>Key Features</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Multispectral Imaging</h3>
        <p>Capture visible, near-infrared, and specialized spectral bands for comprehensive environmental and terrain analysis.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>LiDAR Integration</h3>
        <p>High-density point cloud generation with centimeter-level accuracy for precise 3D modeling and terrain mapping.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Extended Flight Time</h3>
        <p>Up to 50 minutes of operation per charge for covering large survey areas in a single flight.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>GNSS Positioning</h3>
        <p>Multi-constellation satellite receivers with RTK capability for survey-grade accuracy in geographical positioning.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Onboard Processing</h3>
        <p>Real-time data processing capabilities for immediate analysis and quality assessment in the field.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Detailed Specifications</h2>
  
  <h3>Imaging & Sensors</h3>
  <div class="spec-grid">
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Multispectral Camera System</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>High-Resolution RGB: 42MP global shutter sensor for detailed visual imagery</li>
        <li>Multispectral Bands: Red, Green, Blue, Red Edge, Near Infrared (NIR) with individual calibration</li>
        <li>Thermal Imaging: Optional thermal sensor for heat distribution mapping</li>
        <li>Radiometric Calibration: Built-in calibration panel for accurate spectral analysis</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>LiDAR System</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Point Cloud Density: Up to 600,000 points per second</li>
        <li>Range: Effective mapping up to 200m altitude with multiple return capability</li>
        <li>Accuracy: ±3cm vertical and horizontal accuracy under optimal conditions</li>
        <li>Pattern: 360° scanning pattern for comprehensive terrain modeling</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Positioning System</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>GNSS: Multi-constellation (GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, BeiDou) for global operation</li>
        <li>RTK/PPK: Real-time kinematic and post-processed kinematic capabilities</li>
        <li>Base Station Compatibility: Works with industry-standard correction services</li>
        <li>Inertial Measurement: High-precision IMU for accurate positional data even in GPS-challenged environments</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Performance & Operation</h3>
  <div class="spec-grid">
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Flight Characteristics</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Flight Time: Up to 50 minutes with standard payload configuration</li>
        <li>Coverage: Capable of mapping up to 100 hectares per flight at 120m altitude</li>
        <li>Cruise Speed: Optimized at 12 m/s for survey operations with adjustable parameters</li>
        <li>Wind Resistance: Stable operation in winds up to 38 km/h</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Operational Parameters</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Preflight Planning: Automated mission planning with terrain-following capabilities</li>
        <li>Operating Temperature: -10°C to 45°C for versatile deployment across various environments</li>
        <li>IP Rating: IP53 for moderate dust and rain protection</li>
        <li>Maximum Altitude: 4000m ASL with appropriate propeller configuration</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Physical Specifications</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Takeoff Weight: 2.8 kg including standard mapping payload</li>
        <li>Dimensions: 89 × 89 × 25 cm deployed</li>
        <li>Transport Case: Custom hard case with foam inserts for field mobility</li>
        <li>Construction: Carbon fiber frame with weather-resistant components</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Data Processing & Integration</h3>
  <div class="spec-grid">
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Onboard Computing</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Processing Unit: Edge computing system for real-time data preprocessing</li>
        <li>Storage: 1TB high-speed SSD for raw data capture</li>
        <li>Wireless Transfer: High-bandwidth data link for immediate transfer when within range</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Software Suite</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Mission Control: Advanced flight planning with terrain awareness and obstacle avoidance</li>
        <li>Data Processing: Desktop application for comprehensive photogrammetry, point cloud processing, and analysis</li>
        <li>Data Export: Compatible formats for all major GIS, CAD, and specialized survey software</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    
    <div class="spec-card">
      <h4>Integration Capabilities</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>API Access: RESTful APIs for automated workflow integration</li>
        <li>Cloud Processing: Optional cloud services for intensive processing tasks</li>
        <li>Ground Control: Support for traditional ground control points and CORS network integration</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Applications & Use Cases</h2>
  
  <h3>Surveying & Construction</h3>
  <div class="use-case">
    <p><strong>Topographic Surveys:</strong> Generate detailed elevation models and contour maps with centimeter-level precision for project planning and design.</p>
    <p><strong>Construction Monitoring:</strong> Regular site surveys to track progress, calculate volumetric changes, and verify as-built conditions against design specifications.</p>
    <p><strong>Infrastructure Inspection:</strong> Detailed mapping of roads, railways, pipelines, and other linear infrastructure for maintenance planning and condition assessment.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Environmental & Agricultural Applications</h3>
  <div class="use-case">
    <p><strong>Precision Agriculture:</strong> Multispectral analysis for crop health assessment, irrigation planning, and yield optimization using vegetation indices.</p>
    <p><strong>Environmental Monitoring:</strong> Track changes in land use, vegetation health, water resources, and environmental impacts over time.</p>
    <p><strong>Forestry Management:</strong> Tree counting, species identification, biomass estimation, and forest health assessment using specialized algorithms.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Urban Planning & Analysis</h3>
  <div class="use-case">
    <p><strong>3D City Modeling:</strong> Create detailed urban digital twins for planning, visualization, and simulation of urban development projects.</p>
    <p><strong>Cadastral Mapping:</strong> Property boundary surveys and land parcel documentation with high positional accuracy.</p>
    <p><strong>Utilities Mapping:</strong> Combined LiDAR and multispectral imaging to identify and document above-ground utility infrastructure.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Integration Diagram</h3>
  <div class="integration-diagram">
    <pre>
{`
 +---------------------------+         +---------------------------+         +---------------------------+
  |  AstroSurvey Q1 Drone     |  --->   |  Data Processing &        |  --->   |  GIS/CAD/BIM Systems      |
  |  - Sensors & Positioning  |         |  Analysis Software        |         |  & Specialized Software   |
  +---------------------------+         +---------------------------+         +---------------------------+
            |       ^                              |       ^
            |       |                              |       |
            v       |                              v       |
   +-----------------+                 +-------------------------+
   | Data Collection | <------------   | Quality Control &       |
   | & Storage       |                 | Validation Processes    |
   +-----------------+                 +-------------------------+
`}
    </pre>
  </div>

  <h2>Workflow & Deployment</h2>
  
  <h3>Pre-Mission Planning</h3>
  <div class="setup-steps">
    <p><strong>Area Definition:</strong> Outline survey boundaries, set ground sampling distance, and define overlap parameters.</p>
    <p><strong>Flight Parameters:</strong> Configure altitude, speed, and camera settings based on project requirements.</p>
    <p><strong>Ground Control:</strong> Establish ground control points if required for enhanced accuracy.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Field Operation</h3>
  <div class="setup-steps">
    <p><strong>Site Assessment:</strong> Evaluate site conditions, obstacles, and potential interference sources before launch.</p>
    <p><strong>Automated Mission:</strong> Execute pre-planned flight path with real-time monitoring through the control tablet.</p>
    <p><strong>Quality Verification:</strong> Preliminary data check in the field to ensure coverage and data quality before leaving the site.</p>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Data Processing</h3>
  <div class="setup-steps">
    <p><strong>Raw Data Download:</strong> Transfer collected data to the processing workstation.</p>
    <p><strong>Photogrammetric Processing:</strong> Generate orthomosaics, digital surface models, and 3D point clouds from raw imagery.</p>
    <p><strong>Analysis & Export:</strong> Apply specialized algorithms for feature extraction, measurement, and analysis before exporting to client deliverable formats.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Support & Resources</h2>
  
  <h3>Technical FAQs</h3>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <div class="faq-item">
      <p class="faq-question">Q1: What is the typical accuracy of the survey results?</p>
      <p>A1: The AstroSurvey Q1 delivers horizontal and vertical accuracy of ±3cm with RTK enabled and proper ground control point usage. Accuracy can vary based on flight height, environmental conditions, and the quality of correction signals.</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="faq-item">
      <p class="faq-question">Q2: How are the multispectral bands calibrated?</p>
      <p>A2: The system includes a calibrated reflectance panel for pre-flight calibration. Additionally, automatic radiometric calibration is performed during processing using sunlight sensors to compensate for varying light conditions during the survey.</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="faq-item">
      <p class="faq-question">Q3: What file formats are supported for export?</p>
      <p>A3: The processing software supports multiple industry-standard formats including GeoTIFF, LAS/LAZ, XYZ point clouds, DXF, SHP, KML, and mesh formats such as OBJ and 3DS for 3D models.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <h3>Training & Support</h3>
  <div class="contact-info">
    <p><strong>Technical Support:</strong> +1-800-ASTR-OFLY (278-767-359)</p>
    <p><strong>Survey Specialist Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:geospatial@astroflyrobotics.com">geospatial@astroflyrobotics.com</a></p>
    <p><strong>Training Programs:</strong> Certified operator courses available online and in-person</p>
    <p><strong>Knowledge Base:</strong> <a href="https://www.astroflyrobotics.com/survey-support" target="_blank">www.astroflyrobotics.com/survey-support</a></p>
  </div>
</ProductLayout>

<style>
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
  
  .feature-card {
    background-color: white;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);
  }
  
  .use-case {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  
  .use-case p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  
  .use-case strong {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
  
  .setup-steps {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  
  .setup-steps p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  
  .setup-steps strong {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
  
  .integration-diagram pre {
    font-family: monospace;
    white-space: pre;
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    background-color: #f8f9fa;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  
  .contact-info p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
</style>
